    "interpretation":  "In the TB-A08 adversarial three-reference context, explicit reference-role declarations increased mean cross_reference_leakage_control from 2.00 to 4.25, a variant-minus-control difference of +2.25. reference_role_fidelity increased from 1.75 to 4.50 (+2.75). semantic_compliance, aesthetic_quality, and technical_defects were all 5.00 in both conditions, so no observed mean tradeoff appeared on those registered dimensions. The primary replicate distributions were heterogeneous: one control replicate scored 5 while one explicit-role replicate scored 2, so the observed benefit was not uniform across every sample. This replication supports the tested hypothesis in this specific context, while remaining a descriptive small-N result.",
